<p>For people building, modding or talking to Ferrite, the firmware for the RT-950 Pro. The user guide is at
<a href="https://manual.ferritefw.dev">manual.ferritefw.dev</a>; this is the other side.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/dev/building/">Building and flashing</a>: the workspace, tests, images, build features, flashing.</li>
<li><a href="/dev/link-protocol/">Link protocol</a>: the binary protocol on the cable and over Bluetooth, with every constant.</li>
<li><a href="/dev/update-file/">Update file</a>: the <code>.ffw</code> file and the SPI parts.</li>
<li><a href="/dev/codeplug/">Codeplug format</a>: the <code>.ferrite</code> files Console saves.</li>
<li><a href="/dev/terminal-pages/">Terminal pages</a>: the stack language the cable terminal's pages are written in.</li>
<li><a href="/dev/flash-map.html">SPI flash map</a>: the 4 MB chip's layout.</li>
</ul>
<p>Every page is made from the files it describes (each says which), so it matches the firmware it was built with.</p>
